From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:51:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: make a compositor that commits itself do its first
 commit as well.

A new compositor has its first commit to make, as on Windows, so it starts
out changed.  One of a CompositorController asks for it through CommitNeeded
as soon as there is a handler to ask.  One that commits itself queued its
commit only when a change came in and found it unchanged, and a new one is
never unchanged: nothing it was given was ever drawn, and no animation ever
ran, because the frame loop starts from a commit.  It now queues its first
commit when it is created, as it queues every later one.

Office's AirSpace uses controllers for its windows and was unaffected; the
dialogs it draws with a compositor of their own, and any application that
activates Windows.UI.Composition.Compositor directly, were.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3e3e74d96e18913fc0b81db1af812d4800165646)

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c b/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
index 8df6ac76449..e4f250cfa82 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
@@ -1657,6 +1657,11 @@ HRESULT compositor_create( BOOL manual, struct compositor **out )
     compositor->frame_handler.lpVtbl = &frame_handler_vtbl;
     InitializeCriticalSectionEx( &compositor->cs, 0, RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_FORCE_DEBUG_INFO );
     compositor->cs.DebugInfo->Spare[0] = (DWORD_PTR)(__FILE__ ": compositor.cs");
+    /* one that commits itself makes that first commit on its own, as it does every later one; until it has,
+     * a change finds the compositor changed already and queues nothing */
+    compositor_lock( compositor );
+    if (!manual) compositor_queue_work( compositor );
+    compositor_unlock( compositor );
     *out = compositor;
     return S_OK;
 }
